    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look poised for high production today, anchored by **Andy Pages**, who earns our top efficiency rating at 70.07. Facing Kochanowicz and his inflated 5.12 xERA, **Andy Pages** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost. Joining him as a high-conviction start is **Sam Antonacci** (67.66), whose lead-off role against Painter provides substantial volume upside, bolstered by his impressive 0.379 xwOBA. We are also leaning into **Gunnar Henderson** (63.31); while Fisher is a moderately tough arm, **Gunnar Henderson** holds a significant 14% platoon advantage and, crucially for our scarcity strategy, his projected matchup benefits from a slow delivery that positions him well for a stolen base opportunity.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card involved the utility spot, where **Josh Jung** (53.90) just edged out **Brayan Rocchio** (41.36). While **Brayan Rocchio** has the speed profile we covet, his positioning at the bottom of the order significantly hampered his efficiency score, keeping him on the bench in favor of the run-producing potential of **Josh Jung** in the three-hole. Elsewhere, we are cautious about the floor for **Dominic Smith** (42.40); he remains in the lineup to maintain our game caps, but his matchup against Ashcraft is mitigated by a 17% SP skill penalty, making him the most volatile asset in today's rotation. Managers should monitor late-breaking weather reports, as the current projections assume standard conditions for all matchups involving **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Curtis Mead**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Miguel Vargas**, and **Jackson Merrill**.",
